Illustrations in this directory are derived from two CC BY-SA 4.0 symbol sets.

1. OpenMoji — the open-source emoji and icon project (https://openmoji.org)
   Original license: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
   (CC BY-SA 4.0) — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

2. Mulberry Symbols — AAC pictograms by Steve Lee (https://mulberrysymbols.org)
   Copyright 2018–2026 Steve Lee
   Original license: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
   (CC BY-SA 4.0) — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
   Used for: back, bib, glue, kick, neck, pet, tape (see the MULBERRY table in
   scripts/fetch-art.mjs for the exact source files).

These files are ADAPTATIONS: the source SVGs have been recolored
(palette-remapped to a muted warm set) and optimized. Because CC BY-SA 4.0
includes a ShareAlike term, these adaptations are distributed under the same
license, CC BY-SA 4.0.

Attribution (as surfaced in the app's About overlay):
  "Illustrations: OpenMoji & Mulberry Symbols — CC BY-SA 4.0, colors modified"

Hand-drawn note: some SVGs here (block, chin, chip, gate, gong, hit, mop, peg,
rug, shin, shut, top, tube, whip, whisk) are original drawings in the same
flat style, made for this project where neither set has a glyph that reads for
a preschooler. They are released under the same CC BY-SA 4.0 terms for
simplicity.
